{"blocks":[["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-1019","The feature addresses the need for more readable control flow when dealing with multiple optional values or validation chains",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","Context"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-1149","Let-chains were stabilized in Rust 1.64 after being proposed in RFC 2497",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","Context"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-1226","Key Principles",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-1247","Special expression syntax: let PATTERN = EXPR becomes a boolean-producing expression only inside if / while conditions, not a normal statement",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","Key Principles"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-1404","Pattern matching with binding: Each let clause performs pattern matching and introduces bindings that propagate forward through the condition chain and into the body",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","Key Principles"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-1580","Short-circuiting: Like normal boolean expressions, let-chains short-circuit—if any pattern fails to match, evaluation stops and the condition becomes false",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","Key Principles"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-1748","Forward propagation: Bindings from earlier let clauses are available in subsequent clauses and in the body",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","Key Principles"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-1865","Expression-oriented: Let-chains produce boolean values, enabling them to be combined with && and || operators",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","Key Principles"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-1987","Mechanism",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-2003","In the context of if or while conditions, let PATTERN = EXPR evaluates the expression and attempts to match it against the pattern",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","Mechanism"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-2144","If the pattern matches:",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","Mechanism"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-2172","Variables are bound to matched components",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","Mechanism","If the pattern matches:"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-2219","The expression evaluates to true",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","Mechanism","If the pattern matches:"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-2259","Evaluation continues to the next clause",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","Mechanism","If the pattern matches:"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-2304","If the pattern doesn't match:",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","Mechanism"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-2338","The expression evaluates to false",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","Mechanism","If the pattern doesn't match:"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-2379","Short-circuiting occurs (for && chains)",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","Mechanism","If the pattern doesn't match:"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-2426","The condition fails and the body is not executed",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","Mechanism","If the pattern doesn't match:"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-2480","The compiler desugars let-chains into nested match expressions, but the linear syntax is much more readable",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","Mechanism"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-2594","Example desugaring:",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","Mechanism"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-2724","Is conceptually equivalent to:",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","Mechanism","Example desugaring:"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-3045","Examples",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-3060","Basic Let-Chain",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","Examples"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-3481","Without Let-Chains (Nested Approach)",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","Examples"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-3971","Chaining Multiple Patterns",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","Examples"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-4147","Comparison to Python's Walrus Operator",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","Examples"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-4194","Python's walrus operator (:=) provides similar functionality but is binding-only",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","Examples","Comparison to Python's Walrus Operator"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-4282","Rust's let-chains provide binding + structural matching + destructuring",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","Examples","Comparison to Python's Walrus Operator"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-4359","Python example:",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","Examples","Comparison to Python's Walrus Operator"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-4506","Rust equivalent:",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","Examples","Comparison to Python's Walrus Operator"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-4694","Where Let-Chains Work",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-4722","✅ if let conditions",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","Where Let-Chains Work"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-4750","✅ while let conditions",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","Where Let-Chains Work"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-4781","✅ match guards (pattern guards)",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","Where Let-Chains Work"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-4821","❌ Not allowed in general expression contexts (e.g., let x = let ...)",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","Where Let-Chains Work"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-4898","❌ Not allowed in arbitrary boolean expressions outside if/while (e.g., foo && let x = bar)",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","Where Let-Chains Work"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-5001","❌ Not allowed with parentheses (must use if let, not if (let x = y))",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","Where Let-Chains Work"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-5080","Misconceptions",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-5101","Let-chains are just pattern matching → False. They're pattern-matching expressions embedded in boolean expression chains, combining multiple concepts",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","Misconceptions"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-5261","let in conditions is the same as normal let → False. It's special expression syntax that only works in if/while conditions",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","Misconceptions"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-5402","Let-chains are the same as Python's walrus operator → False. Walrus is binding-only; let-chains provide structural matching and destructuring",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","Misconceptions"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-5554","You can use let-chains anywhere → False. They only work in if and while condition expressions",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","Misconceptions"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-5662","Let-chains always improve readability → False. They can hurt readability when bindings are logically independent or when error context is needed",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","Misconceptions"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-5817","When to Use Let-Chains",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-5846","Great for:",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","When to Use Let-Chains"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-5865","Nested Option / Result handling",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","When to Use Let-Chains","Great for:"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-5906","Validation funnels where each step depends on the previous",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","When to Use Let-Chains","Great for:"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-5970","Protocol decoding with multiple optional fields",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","When to Use Let-Chains","Great for:"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-6023","Deeply nested struct access patterns",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","When to Use Let-Chains","Great for:"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-6065","Early bail conditions with binding",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","When to Use Let-Chains","Great for:"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-6105","Replacing nested if let statements that form a \"pyramid of doom\"",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","When to Use Let-Chains","Great for:"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-6177","Avoid when:",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","When to Use Let-Chains"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-6197","Readability suffers from too many chained conditions",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","When to Use Let-Chains","Avoid when:"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-6255","Bindings are logically independent (consider separate if let statements)",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","When to Use Let-Chains","Avoid when:"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-6335","You need error context (use match or let else instead)",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","When to Use Let-Chains","Avoid when:"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-6399","The chain becomes too long or complex",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","When to Use Let-Chains","Avoid when:"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-6442","Mental Model",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-6461","Think of && in let-chains as: \"Proceed only if this expression is true — and bind variables if applicable\"",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","Mental Model"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-6576","Each let clause:",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","Mental Model"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-6599","Performs pattern matching",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","Mental Model","Each let clause:"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-6630","Stops evaluation if it fails (short-circuiting)",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","Mental Model","Each let clause:"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-6683","Introduces new bindings into the rest of the chain and body",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","Mental Model","Each let clause:"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-6748","The whole condition short-circuits like a normal boolean expression chain",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","Mental Model"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-6826","If walrus is \"Assign while testing\", then let-chains are \"Match while testing\"",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview","Mental Model"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-block-6913","Formal Terminology",["Rust Let-Chains Conceptual Overview"]],["Rust/Pattern%20Matching/Let-Chains/","source-b